#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:13
msgid "Today, after 2 years and 10 months of work, we are pleased to announce the release of the Xfce desktop 4.12, a new stable version that supersedes Xfce 4.10."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:15
msgid "This long period can only be explained by how awesome Xfce 4.10 was. But as all things, it needed some refreshing - and for that we saw lots of new contributors providing valuable feedback, features and bugfixes. As always, Xfce follows its steady pace of evolution without revolution that seems to match our users' needs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:17
msgid "In this 4.12 cycle, we mainly focused on polishing our user experience on the desktop and window manager, and on updating some components to take advantage of newly available technologies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:19
msgid "The main highlights of this release are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:21
msgid "The window manager gained a new themable Alt+Tab dialog with optional windows preview and a list mode. Initial Client side decoration support was implemented, window tiling mode was improved providing support for corner-tiling, and a new zooming mode was added. A HiDPI Xfwm theme was also added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:22
msgid "The panel can now intelligently hide itself, supports Gtk3 plugins, and saw lots of its third-party plugins updated to take full advantage of the features added in 4.10."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:23
msgid "The desktop has a new wallpaper settings dialog, per workspace wallpaper support, and better multi-monitor handling. It also supports displaying folder cover art and emblems on icons now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:24
msgid "Our session manager was updated to use logind and/or upower if available for hibernate/suspend support. For portability and to respect our users' choices, fallback modes were implemented relying on os-specific backends."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:25
msgid "Support for multi-monitor use was improved in a new display settings dialog and a quick setup popup on monitor plugging."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:26
msgid "The appearance dialog now showcases previews for icons and themes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:27
msgid "Xfsettingsd now supports libinput."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:28
msgid "Power management was not forgotten: A new panel plugin was created, logind/upower support was added to handle battery/lid/brightness events, and locking via light-locker was implemented. The settings dialog was also revamped, and support for X11 screenblanking was added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:29
msgid "Our file manager, the beloved Thunar, saw an insane amount of improvements: tab support, tons of bug fixes, speed-ups, key shortcuts for custom actions, better naming of file copies and links, nice freespace bar in properties, tweaks for the renamer and other dialogs, improved keyboard navigation, fixes for the treeview pane, better wallpaper support, Gtk3 bookmarks support, multiple file properties... need we say more?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:30
msgid "To prepare the future of Xfce with Gtk3, which no longer requires theme engines, we are stopping the development of our Gtk theme engine, and dropping our Gtk3 engine - theme makers, please update your themes to CSS if you want them to work on the next Xfce version."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:31
msgid "Due to gstreamer1.0 having dropped the mixer-interface entirely, and xfce4-mixer and xfce4-volumed relying on this interface with gstreamer0.10, our mixer application and volume daemon cannot be ported to 1.0 and are consequently not maintained anymore."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:33
msgid "Xfce wouldn't be what it is right now without all its goodies. In this area, we also saw a flurry of activity, most notably:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:35
msgid "Xfburn gained BluRay Disc burning support."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:36
msgid "Task manager UI was totally revamped, and got ported to Gtk3."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:37
msgid "Parole's UI was totally redone, parts of it rewritten with many features added. Furthermore it was ported to Gtk3 and gstreamer1.0."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:38
msgid "Mousepad was totally rewritten and got an initial port to Gtk3."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:39
msgid "Imgur.com support was added to the screenshooter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:40
msgid "A new GNOME-Shell-like dashboard named xfdashboard is now available."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:41
msgid "A new alternative menu for the panel named whiskermenu was added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:42
msgid "The GNOME2 hardware monitor plugin was ported to our panel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:43
msgid "Weather plugin got a totally new user interface with powerful customization options and provides tons of detailed information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:44
msgid "Eyes plugin uses 3D coordinates to calculate its eye position, so even more sometimes scary, sometimes funny eyes will spy on you!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:45
msgid "Netload plugin works with the new udev net interface names and can be configured to show transfer rates in the panel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:46
msgid "Clipboard manager plugin optionally displays a QR code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:47
msgid "Cpufreq plugin now supports the intel pstate driver and can adapt better for different panel sizes and information displayed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:48
msgid "Nearly all plugins have been improved to give the same look and feel and to support the new deskbar panel mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:50
msgid "An online tour of the changes in Xfce 4.12 can be viewed here:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:54
msgid "A detailed overview of the changes between Xfce 4.10 and Xfce 4.12 releases can be found on the following page:"
msgstr ""

#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:60
#, fuzzy
msgid "<http://archive.xfce.org/xfce/4.12>"
msgstr "[Telecargar](http://archive.xfce.org/xfce/4.6.2/)"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:62
msgid "A warm thank you all the contributors, translators and packagers for your efforts in making this release possible. We would also like to thank our fantastic users and occasional contributors who submitted bug reports, helped us find issues and sometimes provided patches. We are currently reviewing all patches sent to us and will include many more fixes to Xfce in the next release. We would also like to thank the many people who donated money to our project via Bounty Source. This will help us meet and hack on Xfce in the future!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1425081600.md:64
msgid "As always, we welcome everyone who would like to contribute to the development of Xfce! You can either [test Xfce](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/building) and [report bugs](https://bugzilla.xfce.org), you can help us with [translations](https://www.transifex.com/tag/xfce/) and [documentation](https://docs.xfce.org), with [usability and user experience](https://wiki.xfce.org/design/start) by packaging Xfce into your distribution, and by [submitting patches](https://wiki.xfce.org/dev/howto/contribute) or entirely new features! You can get in touch with us on the Freenode IRC channel #xfce-dev and our [mailing list](https://mail.xfce.org/mailman/listinfo/xfce4-dev)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:0
msgid "Xfce 4.14 released"
msgstr "Xfce 4.14 publicada"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:7
msgid "Today, after 4 years and 5 months of work, we are pleased to announce the release of the Xfce desktop 4.14, a new stable version that supersedes Xfce 4.12."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:11
msgid "In this 4.14 cycle the main goal was to port all core components to Gtk3 (over Gtk2) and GDBus (over D-Bus GLib). Most components also received GObject Introspection support. Along the way we ended up polishing our user experience, introducing quite a few new features and improvements (read below) and fixings a boatload of bugs (read changelog)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:13
msgid "The **main highlights of this release** are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:15
msgid "The [window manager](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfwm4/start) received a slew of updates and features, including support for VSync (using either Present or OpenGL as backend) to reduce or remove display flickering, HiDPI support, improved GLX support with NVIDIA proprietary/closed source drivers, support for XInput2, various compositor improvements and a new default theme."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:16
msgid "The [panel](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-panel/start) got support for RandR's primary monitor feature, improved window grouping in the tasklist plugin (better UX, visual group indicator etc), a per-panel \"icon-size\" setting, a new default clock format and clock format evaluator as well as an improved default panel layout."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:17
msgid "The [desktop](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfdesktop/start) now has support for RandR's primary monitor feature, an orientation option for icon arrangement, a \"Next Background\" context menu option to advance the wallpaper and it now syncs the user's wallpaper selection to AccountsService."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:18
msgid "A completely new settings dialog to [manage color profiles](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-settings/color) has been created. For most users this means out of the box support for color-managed printing (through cupsd) and scanning (through saned). For monitor profiles you will have to install an additional service like xiccd."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:19
msgid "The [display dialog](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-settings/display) received a lot of attention during this cycle and a big feature: Users are now able to save and (automatically) restore complete multi-display configurations, which is especially helpful for those who frequently connect their laptop to varying docking stations or setups. Furthermore a lot of time was spent on making the user interface more intuitive and a hidden option was added to support RandR display scaling (configured via Xfconf)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:20
msgid "We added an option to enable Gtk window scaling to the [appearance dialog](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-settings/appearance) and a monospace font option as well. However we had to drop theme previews as they didn't produce consistent results with Gtk3."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:21
msgid "While we decided to drop splash screens from the [session manager](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-session/start), we added lots of features and fixes instead. Among them are hybrid sleep support, improvements to the default session startup avoiding race conditions, a feature to add and edit autostart entries, a switch user button in the logout dialog and improved session chooser and settings dialogs (the latter with a new tab that shows saved sessions). Furthermore you can now run commands not only \"autostart style\" at login time, but also when your computer suspends, logs out etc. Finally Gtk applications are now session-managed over DBus and screensavers are also communicated with (e.g. inhibited) over DBus."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:22
msgid "As always, [Thunar](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/thunar/start) - our file manager - received a lot of features and fixes. Among the visible changes are the completely reworked pathbar, support for larger thumbnails as well as support for a \"folder.jpg\" file altering the folder's icon (e.g. for music album covers). Power users will also notice the improved keyboard navigation (zooming, tab navigation). Thunar's volume manager has gained Bluray support."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:23
msgid "Our [thumbnailing service tumbler](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/thunar/tumbler) received a lot of fixes and support for the Fujifilm RAF format."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:24
msgid "The [application finder](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-appfinder/start) can now optionally be opened as a single window and can now be more easily navigated with the keyboard only."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:25
msgid "The [power manager](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-power-manager/start) received a lot of bugfixes and some smaller features, including support for the XF86Battery button and for the newly created xfce4-screensaver. The panel plugin also saw several improvements: it can now optionally show the remaining time and/or percentage and it now relies on UPower's standard icon names to work with more icon themes out of the box. With LXDE moving on to a QT base the LXDE panel plugin was dropped."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:27
msgid "A lot of **applications and plugins** that are part of the Xfce eco-system - often dubbed \"goodies\" - are part of what makes Xfce great. A lot of those have also seen important changes along the timeline of the 4.14 release. To highlight a few:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:29
msgid "Our [notification service](https://docs.xfce.org/apps/notifyd/start) has gained support for persistence - in other words: notification logging - and a \"Do Not Disturb\" mode, which suppresses all notifications. A new panel plugin was created that shows missed notifications (especially helpful during \"Do Not Disturb\" mode) and gives quick access to toggling \"Do Not Disturb\" mode. Finally support for showing notifications on RandR's primary monitor was added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:30
msgid "Our media player [Parole](https://docs.xfce.org/apps/parole/start) received improved support for network streams and podcasts, as well as a new \"mini mode\" and automatic choosing of the best available video backend. Furthermore it also inhibits both screensavers and power managers during video playback now, making sure users don't have to go wiggle their mouse periodically while enjoying a movie."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:31
msgid "Our image viewer [Ristretto](https://docs.xfce.org/apps/ristretto/start) has seen various user interface improvements and support for setting the desktop wallpaper. It has recently also seen its first Gtk3-based development release."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:32
msgid "The [screenshooter](https://docs.xfce.org/apps/screenshooter/start) now allows users to move the selection rectangle and at the same time displays its width and height. The imgur upload dialog was revamped and the command line allows for more flexibility."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:33
msgid "Our [clipboard manager](https://docs.xfce.org/panel-plugins/clipman/start) now has improved keyboard shortcut support (through a port to GtkApplication), improved and more consistent icon sizing as well as a new application icon."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:34
msgid "The [pulseaudio panel plugin](https://docs.xfce.org/apps/pulseaudio-plugin/start) received MPRIS2 support to be able to remotely control media players and desktop-wide multimedia key support, essentially rendering xfce4-volumed-pulse a superfluous additional daemon."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:35
msgid "And finally the [terminal emulator](https://docs.xfce.org/apps/terminal/start) saw a huge amount of bug fixes and improvements since Xfce 4.12."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:37
msgid "There is also a group of **new projects** that have become part of our project. Say hi to:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:39
msgid "We finally have our own [screensaver](https://docs.xfce.org/apps/screensaver/start) (yes - we realize it's 2019 ;)). With lots of features and tight Xfce integration (obviously) it is a great addition to our catalog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:40
msgid "The [status notifier panel plugin](https://goodies.xfce.org/projects/panel-plugins/xfce4-statusnotifier-plugin) provides a next-generation system tray where applications can show indicators. It supersedes the Ubuntu-centric xfce4-indicator-plugin for most application indicators."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:41
msgid "[Catfish file search](https://docs.xfce.org/apps/catfish/start) is like an old friend for most Xfce users - now it's officially part of Xfce!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:42
msgid "Finally [Panel Profiles](https://git.xfce.org/apps/xfce4-panel-profiles/about/), which allows you to backup and restore your panel layouts, has moved under the Xfce umbrella."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:44
msgid "As always it’s also time to say goodbye to some older **unmaintained or deprecated projects**. (Luckily our projects only go to the attic aka the archive on git.xfce.org when they die.) With a salty teardrop of sadness we bid farewell to:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:46
msgid "garcon-vala, gtk-xfce-engine, pyxfce, thunar-actions-plugin, xfbib, xfc, xfce4-kbdleds-plugin, xfce4-mm, xfce4-taskbar-plugin, xfce4-windowlist-plugin, xfce4-wmdock-plugin and xfswitch-plugin"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:48
msgid "An online tour of the changes in Xfce 4.14 can be viewed here:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:52
msgid "A detailed overview of the changes between Xfce 4.12 and Xfce 4.14 releases can be found on the following page:"
msgstr ""

#: content/about/news/1565568000.md:58
#, fuzzy
msgid "<http://archive.xfce.org/xfce/4.14>"
msgstr "[Telecargar](http://archive.xfce.org/xfce/4.6.1/)"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:0
msgid "Xfce 4.16 released"
msgstr "Xfce 4.16 publicada"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:7
msgid "Today, after 1 year and 4 months of work, we are happy to announce the release of the Xfce desktop 4.16, a new stable version that supersedes Xfce 4.14."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:11
msgid "4.16 was a special cycle in many respects (not only pandemic-wise, but also). One of the corner-stones of the non-code changes concerns our migration to GitLab, which is a change in development workflow and a huge step forward in terms of becoming more contributor-friendly and welcoming. In parts, the [humungous changelog of Xfce 4.16](https://www.xfce.org/download/changelogs/4.16) can be attributed to new contributors proposing merge requests (288 merge requests were merged or closed against our core components alone!). We also created a reference Docker container ([xfce/xfce-build](https://hub.docker.com/r/xfce/xfce-build)) and added CI pipelines to all components to ensure we don´t break the build. None of this would have been possible without our hosting being sponsored by [Gandi](https://gandi.net) and [Fosshost](https://fosshost.org)!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:13
msgid "Another big change concerns our visual identity, which we updated from a strange mix of random (partly Tango-based) icons and not following any naming scheme to a new, visually consistent set (following the freedesktop.org naming specification and a fixed color palette). We´re aware this will generate some work for icon theme maintainers (if they really want to override our gorgeous icons ;)) but we believe the longterm benefit outweighs this one-time effort."
msgstr ""

#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:15
msgid "<img src=\"//cdn.xfce.org/about/tour/4.16/upstream-icons.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"upstream-icons\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:17
msgid "And then finally we did some housekeeping (e.g. by dropping Gtk2 support code) and we also added features and improvements - all while sticking to a reasonable release cycle timeframe."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:19
msgid "So without further ado, here go the **main highlights of this release**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:21
msgid "The [window manager](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfwm4/start) received lots of updates and improvements again in the area of compositing and GLX. If a primary display was set, the alt-tab dialog will now only be shown there. Furthermore some handy new options to zoom the cursor along with rest of the display as well as an option to keep minimized windows in the most recently used list complement this release."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:22
msgid "We added a new plugin to the [panel](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-panel/start) dubbed “statustray” which combines both StatusNotifier and legacy Systray items. An animated autohide transition now clearly shows the user “where the panel has gone” and a dark mode (enabled by default) makes the panel drop into the background a bit more with bright themes like the Gtk default Adwaita. Quite a few more smaller improvements were also introduced like accessing desktop actions from a Launcher´s right-click menu, the Window Buttons plugin now offering to `Launch a new instance` of an application and the Workspace Switcher now optionally showing automatic numbering for workspaces."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:23
msgid "Support for fractional scaling was added to the [display dialog](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-settings/display), along with highlighting the preferred mode of a display with an asterisk and adding aspect ratios next to resolutions. Falling back to a working mode after misconfiguring the display layout has also been made more robust."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:24
msgid "A new tab in the “About Xfce” dialog shows basic system information like CPU or GPU type. Furthermore the layout and visuals of the dialog were improved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:25
msgid "The [settings manager](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-settings/start) has improved search and filter capabilities. Furthermore all settings dialogs now use window decorations drawn by Gtk (client side decorations)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:26
msgid "The “Mime Settings” and “Preferred Applications” dialogs were merged into the “Default Applications” dialog - making it easier for users to set which application handles which filetype or action from one place."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:27
msgid "Our file manager [Thunar](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/thunar/start) received a boatload of fixes and quite a few notable features, including pause for copy/move operations, support for queued file transfer, remembering view settings per directory and support for transparency in Gtk themes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:28
msgid "Our [thumbnailing service tumbler](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/thunar/tumbler) became more flexible by being able to exclude paths. Furthermore support for .epub (e-book format) was added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:29
msgid "The [session manager](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-session/start) offers improved support for GPG agent 2.1 and the setting dialog was visually improved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:30
msgid "The [power manager](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-power-manager/start) received a lot of bugfixes and some smaller features - among them a cleanup of its settings dialog, an optional visual indicator for when `Presentation Mode` is enabled, more accurate battery status icons and automatically dismissing low-power notifications upon the connection of a charger."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:31
msgid "The [desktop](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfdesktop/start) mostly received bugfixes and small improvements - and the new default wallpaper!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:32
msgid "Our menu library [garcon](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/garcon/start) received new APIs and now doesn´t launch applications as children of the process hosting the menu anymore. The previous behavior led to applications crashing along with e.g. the panel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:33
msgid "The [applicaton finder](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-appfinder/start) now allows for sorting applications by “frecency” - a combination of frequency and recency."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:34
msgid "Dependency updates: Drop Gtk2, add LibGTop, bump Gtk &gt;= 3.22, GLib and GDBus &gt;= 2.50"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:36
msgid "An online tour of the changes in Xfce 4.16 can be viewed here:"
msgstr ""

#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:38
msgid "<https://www.xfce.org/about/tour416>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:40
msgid "A detailed overview of the changes between Xfce 4.14 and Xfce 4.16 releases can be found on the following page:"
msgstr ""

#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:42
msgid "<https://www.xfce.org/download/changelogs/4.16>"
msgstr ""

#: content/about/news/1608595200.md:46
#, fuzzy
msgid "<https://archive.xfce.org/xfce/4.16>"
msgstr "[Telecargar](http://archive.xfce.org/xfce/4.6.2/)"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/about/news/1671062400.md:0
msgid "Xfce 4.18 released"
msgstr "Xfce 4.18 publicada"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1671062400.md:7
msgid "After almost two years of work, we are happy to announce the release of Xfce 4.18 !"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1671062400.md:11
msgid "Since Xfce 4.16 a lot of major development happened. Our team added multiple nice new features, did a gazillion of bug fixes and did various minor improvements. Finally, all that is going to be released for your pleasure."
msgstr ""

#: content/about/news/1671062400.md:13
msgid "<img src=\"//cdn.xfce.org/about/screenshots/4.18-1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Xfce 4.18 screenshot\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/news/1671062400.md:15
msgid "This development cycle was influenced a lot by [GSoC 2021](https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2021/organizations/5706869816950784) and [GSoC 2022](https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/programs/2022/organizations/xfce), which led to various new features, most of them for Thunar, the Xfce File Manager. Though as well multiple other Xfce components got a lot of love and many improvements were done under the hood."
msgstr ""

